--TEST--
A `throw` through a `?Throwable` holding `null` raises PHP's own "Can only throw objects" — `rule:errors/propagation`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `null` is the one tag a `?Throwable` can carry that is not an object, and
// the raise is catchable like any other rather than a fatal.
?Throwable $empty = null;

try {
    throw $empty;
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "caught: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

echo "after\n";
--EXPECT--
caught: Can only throw objects
after
